tests/golden/check/threads-neither-type-reaches-c.hero:11:14: error[ffi_field_type]: `(mailbox i64)` cannot be a field of a `record` in an `extern` group — the header owns the layout, and it can hold a number, `bool`, `ptr`, `cstr`, or another record of the group (spec § 13)
tests/golden/check/threads-neither-type-reaches-c.hero:12:21: error[ffi_type]: `(mailbox i64)` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s parameter — a C header can declare a number, `bool`, `str`, `ptr`, `cstr`, a function type as a parameter, and a `record` declared in this same group (spec § 13)
tests/golden/check/threads-neither-type-reaches-c.hero:13:30: error[ffi_type]: `(thread i64)` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s result — a C header can declare a number, `bool`, `str`, `ptr`, `cstr`, a function type as a parameter, and a `record` declared in this same group (spec § 13)
tests/golden/check/threads-neither-type-reaches-c.hero:14:55: error[ffi_type]: `(function((thread i64), ptr) -> i32)` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s parameter — the callback may stand there, but `(thread i64)` inside it cannot (spec § 13)
